Write video output as a raw NUT clip, and take it where no encoder exists

The mp4 and mov muxer sits inside one canImport(AVFoundation) block, so
generate --output clip.mp4 hard-errors off Darwin, and the suggested PNG
fallback silently drops the audio tensor.

--output clip.nut now writes the clip raw on every platform. One file holds
rgb48le video, pcm_f32le stereo audio, and an info packet carrying the prompt,
model and seed. ffmpeg, ffplay and mpv read it directly, so it is also the
lossless source for whatever encoder you prefer. Where AVFoundation is absent
the #else writes that same file, taking the .nut extension in place of the one
given.
